{{!
    @template tool_vae/situation_facts

    The lines that say a situation, in a block: each line with its label in grey when it has one, a line break between two
    lines (never after the last). The block is drawn even with no line.

    Every text comes from the context, already worded by tool_vae\output\situation_facts. The template holds no logic.
    Every value is escaped (double braces): none of them is HTML.

    Classes required for JS:
    * none

    Data attributes required for JS:
    * none

    Context variables required for this template:
    * class - string, the classes of the block
    * lines - array: sep (bool, a break before the line), label (object: words) or null, text

    Example context (json):
    {
        "class": "small",
        "lines": [
            {"sep": false, "label": {"words": "Period"}, "text": "1 September 2025 - 23 June 2026"},
            {"sep": true, "label": null, "text": "2 pieces"}
        ]
    }
}}
<div class="{{class}}">{{#lines}}{{#sep}}<br>{{/sep}}{{#label}}<span class="text-muted me-2">{{words}}</span>{{/label}}{{!
}}{{text}}{{/lines}}</div>
